                <pb facs="0592" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg512"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Lord
                            Lansdowne.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-02-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Under instructions from my Government,
                    I have the honor to inclose herewith for your lordship’s information a copy of a
                    memorandum expressing the views of the United States in regard to the proposed
                    convention and arrangement between the Chinese and Russian Governments
                    respecting Manchuria, which has been telegraphed to our legation at Pekin and to
                    our embassy at St. Petersburg.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
